// PFXIsPFXBlob oracle probe (crypt32.dll). Each case is a hex blob; the probe
// prints "<case>\t<BOOL return>\t<GetLastError after, prefilled 0xDEADBEEF>".
// The NULL-pointer cases run in a child process each and report its exit code
// (0xC0000005 = access violation).
//
// Build (from the repo root):
//   x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -O1 -o pfx64.exe tests/winapi/crypt32/oracle/pfx_is_pfx_blob_probe.c -lcrypt32
//   i686-w64-mingw32-gcc   -O1 -o pfx32.exe tests/winapi/crypt32/oracle/pfx_is_pfx_blob_probe.c -lcrypt32
// Run on winoracle; save stdout as pfx_is_pfx_blob_probe{64,32}.expected.
// gen_pfx_is_pfx_blob_oracle.py turns the cases + outputs into the test .inc.
//
// real_pfx / real_pfx_nomac / pkcs7_signed / x509_cert were made with OpenSSL
// 3 (prime256v1 self-signed "CN=vpfx"; pkcs12 -export with and without
// -nomac; crl2pkcs7 -nocrl). The other cases are hand-built DER variants.
